# FINAL LOCKED LOGIN PAGE — DO NOT MODIFY WITHOUT EXPLICIT USER APPROVAL

The Login Page is an approved, frozen baseline. Do not change, redesign, remove, add, resize, reposition, restyle, or restyle-via-globals anything on it unless the user explicitly requests that specific Login Page change.

## Locked files (do not edit without explicit approval)

- `04_Frontend/frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.tsx`
- `04_Frontend/frontend/src/pages/login-page.css`
- `04_Frontend/frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.test.tsx`
- `04_Frontend/frontend/public/krishna.png` (and other login background assets)

Preserve exactly: background image, zoom, position, quality, layout, branding, Gujarati/English/Sanskrit copy, icons, login card, colors, fonts, spacing, borders, buttons, inputs, responsive rules, and auth functionality.

## Other work must stay independent

Work on dashboards, routes, modules, and shared components without touching the files above.

If you must change shared CSS (for example `.input-field`, `.btn-primary`) or layout shells:

- Do not alter `.dhara-login` or `login-page.css`.
- Scope new styles so they cannot override `.dhara-login` descendants.
- Prefer new class names over changing globals used by the login form.

## Allowed exception

Only modify the Login Page when the user clearly asks for a specific login-page change in that conversation.
